# Frontend (`fe`): Vercel React & composition skills

When editing, reviewing, or writing code under `fe/`, **read and follow** the skills below. Canonical copy in the repo: **`.agents/skills/`** (duplicated under `.claude/skills/`).

## Required for React / component architecture

1. **`/.agents/skills/vercel-react-best-practices/SKILL.md`** — start here; full detail in **`AGENTS.md`** in the same folder and files under `rules/`.
2. **`/.agents/skills/vercel-composition-patterns/SKILL.md`** — compound components, context, avoid boolean-prop sprawl; detail in **`AGENTS.md`** and `rules/`.
3. **`/.agents/skills/shadcn-tailwind/SKILL.md`** — shadcn/ui, Tailwind v4, CVA, `fe/components.json` aliases, CLI adds, tokens in `index.css`; use with the React and composition skills above.

The `fe` stack is **Vite + React** (not Next.js): apply **client**, **bundle**, **rerender**, **rendering**, **js**, and **composition** guidance where it fits; skip or adapt **Next.js/RSC-only** rules (e.g. `server-*`, App Router–style `async-api-routes`) when they do not apply.

## UI / accessibility / UX (when the task is relevant)

4. **`/.agents/skills/web-design-guidelines/SKILL.md`** — follow the file’s workflow (fetch guidelines when auditing UI).

## How to work

- Prefer **SKILL.md** first for categories; open **AGENTS.md** or individual **`rules/*.md`** files when you need concrete examples.
- Do not paste long skill text into this rule; always reference the paths above.
